# Cloudflare Pages response headers (this file ships in the build output; Pages reads it at serve time).
# HSTS: browsers pin HTTPS for 180 days after one visit. Deliberately conservative — no
# includeSubDomains (future subdomains stay unconstrained) and no preload (a one-way door).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000

# Fonts. Pages' default is `max-age=14400, must-revalidate` — a 4-hour TTL, so a returning reader
# re-validates (a full round trip) twice a day and re-enters the font race every time. These three
# files change roughly never, so cache them for a year and skip revalidation entirely.
#
# ⚠️ THE FILENAMES ARE NOT CONTENT-HASHED (they live in public/, which Nuxt copies verbatim). With
# `immutable`, a browser that has one WILL NOT re-fetch it for a year, so editing the bytes in place
# would strand every existing visitor on the old face. RULE: change a font file → change its name,
# and update both main.css and the preloads in nuxt.config.ts.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
